## 🧠 Featured DAX Formulations & Data Modeling
To handle large insurance volumes and support dynamic time-intelligence analysis without performance degradation, I developed highly optimized DAX measures. Below are 4 core advanced formulations implemented in this project:


### 1. Cumulative Budget Premium (BP YTD)
*Computes the year-to-date cumulative budget premium volume, dynamically shifting based on the selected calendar periods.*
```dax
Budget_Premium_YTD = 
VAR DATEEND= DATE(YEAR([START]),12,31)
VAR DATESTART= DATE(YEAR([START]),1,1)
RETURN

CALCULATE(
[BUDGET_PREMIUM],
ALL(Calendar[Date]),
Calendario[Calendar]>=DATESTART,
Calendario[Calendar]<=DATEEND
)

```

### 2. Distinct Policy Counter
*Computes the number of policies which Premium es above 0, tu exclude canceled Policies.*
```dax
COUNT_POLICIES = CALCULATE(DISTINCTCOUNT(Produccion[POLIZA]),Produccion[PRIMA_PERIODO]>0)
```

### 3. Prior Period Premium
*Computes last period premium for comparision.*
```dax
Prior_Period_Premium = CALCULATE(SUM(Production[PERIOD_PREMIUM]),dateadd(Calendar[Date],-1,YEAR))
```

### 4. Agent Ranking
*Creates a ranking for agents based on their Premium. It helps creating simple tables that shows only the most important information,*
```dax
Rank Agente = 
IF (
    ISINSCOPE( Production[NAME_AGT_1] ),
    RANKX (
        CALCULATETABLE (
            VALUES ( Production[NAME_AGT_1] ),
            ALLSELECTED ( Production[NAME_AGT_1])
        ),
        [PERIOD_PREMIUM]
    )
)
```

### 5. PREMIUM SEGMENTS
*Creates a variable that enables to create filter that segments the shown information. It can be used to create client profiles with several conditions.*
```dax
PREMIUM_OVER_10K = 
CALCULATE(SUM('Production'[Prima Periodo]),
'Production'[PERIOD_PREMIUM]>10000)
```